SDL2: one button, every output a mapping binds it to

HandleJoystickButton stops at the first binding of a button, so a mapping
can't make one button two things. ChaOS's mapping for the TrimUI Brick, which
has no stick, makes the d-pad both the d-pad and the left stick
(res/ports/run.sh), so that a port steering with a stick can be played.

ChaOS, for ports only (src/ports.h). After plastron's 0001 and 0002.

diff --git a/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c b/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c
index 36e521e..8fa2fac 100644
--- a/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c
+++ b/src/joystick/SDL_gamecontroller.c
@@ -267,7 +267,7 @@ static void HandleJoystickButton(SDL_GameController *gamecontroller, int button,
             } else {
                 SDL_PrivateGameControllerButton(gamecontroller, binding->output.button, state);
             }
-            break;
+            /* ChaOS: on to the next binding of the same button, if any */
         }
     }
 }
